# BotRoyale — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
NestJS backend + React/Vite/Tailwind frontend for a competitive poker bot platform.
All frontend styles are **inline** (`style={{ ... }}`), no CSS modules.
Design tokens live in the `C` object per file (or imported from `frontend/src/styles/tokens.ts`).
Font is always `'Trebuchet MS', sans-serif`.

---

## CRITICAL: Onboarding Flow Protection

> Any changes to `App.tsx`, `Home.tsx`, `Sidebar.tsx`, or global styling **must** verify that the
> `WelcomeCarousel` (Onboarding) remains functional. Specifically:
>
> 1. **localStorage gate** — The key `'hasSeenWelcomeCarousel'` must never be cleared, bypassed,
>    or overwritten by unrelated code. Only `WelcomeCarousel`'s own close/upgrade handlers
>    (via `Home.tsx`'s `handleCarouselClose` / `handleCarouselUpgrade`) may write this key.
>
> 2. **Visibility condition** — `Home.tsx` renders `<WelcomeCarousel>` only when:
>    - `showCarousel === true` (derived from `localStorage.getItem('hasSeenWelcomeCarousel') !== 'true'`)
>    - AND `user !== null` (authenticated user present from `useAuthStore`)
>    Do not add additional guards that could silently prevent first-time users from seeing it.
>
> 3. **Theme consistency** — All four carousel slides use Cyan (`#00e5ff`) as the primary accent
>    and Zinc-dark (`#0d0d22` / `#1e1e3f`) as backgrounds. If the global accent color token
>    changes, update `WelcomeCarousel.tsx`'s local `C` object to match.
>
> 4. **Prop interface stability** — `WelcomeCarousel` accepts:
>    - `userName: string`
>    - `onClose: (persist: boolean) => void`
>    - `onUpgrade: (persist: boolean) => void`
>    Do not rename or remove these props without updating `Home.tsx` and the test suite.
>
> **Before merging any PR that touches the above files, manually verify:**
> - Clear localStorage → load Dashboard → carousel appears on slide 1
> - Set `localStorage.setItem('hasSeenWelcomeCarousel', 'true')` → reload → carousel absent
> - Check "Don't show again" + click "Build Your First Bot" → carousel absent on next load

---

## Frontend Conventions

- **Styles:** Always inline (`style={{ ... }}`). Never add CSS modules or class-based styling.
- **Design tokens:** Use the `C` object. If a file doesn't have one, import from `../styles/tokens`.
- **Sidebar:** Use `<Sidebar />` from `../components/Sidebar` with no props. Never inline a sidebar.
- **Auth state:** `useAuthStore` from `../store/authStore` — `{ user, token, isAuthenticated }`.
- **API client:** `api` from `../lib/axios` (auto-injects JWT, base URL from `VITE_API_URL`).
- **Routing:** React Router v6. Protected routes use `<ProtectedRoute>` wrapper in `App.tsx`.
- **Zustand stores:** `authStore`, `sidebarStore`, `analyticsStore` — use `persist` middleware for durable state.
- **No `Math.random()` in game logic.** All randomness uses the provably fair HMAC-SHA256 chain or `crypto.randomBytes`.

---

## Backend Conventions

- **Auth:** JWT in `Authorization: Bearer {token}` header. Guards: `JwtAuthGuard`, `RolesGuard`.
- **Global prefix:** `api/v1` — all REST endpoints under `http://localhost:3000/api/v1`.
- **Tournament statuses:** `registering | running | final_table | finished | cancelled`. No `pending` or `upcoming`.
- **Entities:** Always export from `src/entities/index.ts`. Always export repos from `src/repositories/index.ts`.
- **Migrations:** Run `npm run migration:run` after adding entities. File naming: `{timestamp}-{PascalCaseName}.ts`.

---

## Testing

- Frontend: Vitest + React Testing Library (`npm test` in `frontend/`).
- Backend: Vitest unit tests in `tests/unit/`, e2e in `tests/e2e/`.
- Game logic: `npm run test:poker -- --games=100 --bots=8` after any game engine change.
- TypeScript: `npx tsc --noEmit` in `frontend/` must pass before every PR.

---

## Documentation Updates (Required)

After any non-trivial change:
1. **New API endpoint** → update `docs/API.md`
2. **Feature change/removal** → update `CLAUDE.md`
3. **Major UI change** → update `CLAUDE.md` (GameSpectator section if relevant)
4. **Security decisions** → update `docs/SECURITY.md`
5. **Onboarding changes** → update `docs/onboarding.md`
